# Caddy config for the living app.
#
# Behind Cloudflare (when the deployment was created with a CF zone token):
#   - Rate limiting lives at the CF edge, keyed on the REAL client IP (set up
#     at init via the Cloudflare Rulesets API — see src/lib/dns.ts). The
#     previous `key {remote_host}` would otherwise see CF's edge IP shared
#     across thousands of users, throttling legit users and multiplying
#     attacker throughput across PoPs.
#   - Authenticated Origin Pulls: CF presents a client cert signed by CF's
#     Origin Pull CA on every origin connection. Caddy requires+verifies it
#     (the `tls { client_auth { ... } }` block below is rendered for CF-fronted
#     deployments; empty otherwise), so a direct hit on the VPS IP — bypassing
#     CF and its edge rate limit — fails the TLS handshake before any HTTP
#     happens. No CF-IP allowlist to maintain.
#
# Direct deployments (operator did NOT add a CF zone token — free sslip.io
# hostnames, or BYO domain with manual DNS) ship without rate limiting and
# without origin-pull enforcement.
longlivethis.site {
  tls {
    client_auth {
      mode require_and_verify
      trusted_ca_cert_file /etc/caddy/cloudflare-origin.pem
    }
  }
  reverse_proxy localhost:3000
  encode gzip
}